diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index b1541decc3..4dc6819e05 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -496,7 +496,15 @@ factual: paths, commands, invariants — no essays.
   addressable: real JSONL child sessions, `task_status`/`task_observe`/
   `task_send`/`task_cancel` (model-facing job abort), child-only `reply` +
   sibling `agent_message` (pending-queue + hop-capped),
-  `completed_without_reply` notice. Child IDENTITY for tool calls is
+  `completed_without_reply` notice. gh-1948: the executor flushes each
+  child's transcript at every turn boundary (the JSONL exists and grows
+  mid-run), and `task_observe` resolves a placeholder-handle child
+  (`<parentSessionId>/<id>` until the first flush) through
+  `resolveChildSessionPath` (`child_session_io.dart` — the sessions-tree
+  header scan) wired by the CLI via `SubagentServices.resolveChildSessionPath`,
+  healing the handle onto the real path; read failures degrade to a
+  structured "no transcript available yet"/"transcript unavailable"
+  message, never an uncaught exception. Child IDENTITY for tool calls is
   zone-scoped (`subagent_scope.dart`, gh-970): `runSpawn`/`resumeChild`
   publish the running child's id via `runWithSubagentScope`, and
   `TaskExecutor.currentSubagentId` reads the zone FIRST — the executor's
diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 95106eb884..529f613c10 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -13,6 +13,19 @@ block a release again.

 ## Unreleased

+- fix(gh-1948): `task_observe` works on a RUNNING background subagent
+  instead of crashing with an uncaught `SessionException` on the
+  `<parentSessionId>/<agentName>` placeholder. Three legs: the executor
+  flushes each child's transcript incrementally at every turn boundary
+  (the JSONL exists and grows mid-run — also crash-resilience for
+  aborted children), `task_observe` resolves a placeholder handle's real
+  session file from the sessions tree (the same `agent: subagent` /
+  `parent:` / `id:` header scan the boot adoption uses) and heals the
+  handle onto the found path, and every read failure degrades to a
+  structured "transcript unavailable" / "no transcript available yet"
+  message instead of an uncaught tool error. The child-transcript reader
+  rides the transient-ENOENT retry (issue #427) — it reads while the
+  executor appends.
 - fix(#1941): the selected CodeMie project now rides EVERY model request.
   The header is baked into `Model.headers` only by the connect-time
   switches (gh-1809), so every other rebuild silently dropped
